libqxp is a library and a set of tools for reading and converting
QuarkXPress file format. It supports versions 3.1-4.1 currently.

libqxp requires boost, icu and librevenge to build.

Conversion tools:

- qxp2svg, qxp2text, qxp2raw: convert through librevenge.
- qxp2openlayout: converts a document to OpenLayout 0.4 JSON
  (https://github.com/signalwerk/spec.OpenLayout), keeping its structure:
  master pages, paragraph and character stylesheets, the color list and
  linked text chains. Data the OpenLayout spec doesn't cover yet is written
  with the "qxd:" namespace prefix, as the spec provides for extensions.
  Styles live directly in defs, with shared UX:type authoring categories and
  UX:next paragraph-style links. A qxd:settings
  style supplies body defaults. Script metrics use reusable fontSize/transform
  styles; unitless path coordinates always use CSS pixels, independent of --unit.
  Run "qxp2openlayout --help" for options.

The library is available under MPL 2.0+.
